WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:06.100
Zeolite 13X, both records measured up to 1 bar. Is the CO₂/N₂ selectivity at least 300?

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:11.600
Well-fitting models answer 217 to 2,018. The tables alone cannot decide: UNDETERMINED.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:17.400
The advice: measure N₂ above 1 bar. More CO₂ points are predicted to change nothing.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:24.500
Add the real CO₂ measurements up to 10 bar: the interval does not move.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:28.800
Now add the real N₂ measurements, a few points at a time.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:34.800
With N₂ measured to 10 bar the interval is 13 times narrower and the answer is a certain YES.
